    "staticCounterexample": "With unchanged local actor/client/read sources, submit expectedVersion7 and topics:[]; accept a shape-valid exact-client response with version8, one retained topic and rejected:{topics:[],terms:[]}. The current parser checks only association and next version; execute then clears the unknown fence, caches the contradictory targeting and closes. This is a source-derived counterexample, not an executed browser reproduction.",
    "nativeInference": "Because native getWatchlist reads the head and topic/term projections in separate withTenant calls after the write transaction, an intervening writer can change topic data between those reads. A next-version head alone does not prove the topic projection belongs to this submitted replacement. This concurrency mechanism is inferred from the retrieved code, not observed in a live environment.",
    "boundedRestart": [
      "Preserve this exact source/evidence checkpoint and add a synthetic remove-all-topics/retained-topic next-version baseline; also characterize simple edited-label/old-projection handling. Do not send live writes.",
      "Keep exact client and next-version checks, but require the returned accepted targeting projection to be attributable to the submitted full replacement using the published normalization and actual rejection details. Preserve native topic index/termType rejection association fields where needed; do not invent IDs or a transaction receipt.",
      "A contradictory or unattributable receipt must retain the current draft and unknown fence, avoid success-close and accepted-target cache publication, and offer only the existing explicit saved-value reload. Reload does not prove rollback or permit automatic replay.",
      "Retain all existing Core projection, Intel version conflict/428, rename/partial-rejection, actor/source/lifetime/close and no-replay assertions. Add correct normalized/empty replacement and existing legitimate partial-rejection acceptance alongside the mismatch regressions. Run only focused affected cases before the eventual final combined gate."
